  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5774bd79aa42c7f42b20b5b97d4c619d, type: 3}
  m_Name: lv2_mc_collateral
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Cardio.Data.PuzzleData
  PuzzleId: lv2_mc_collateral
  Type: 4
  Complexity: 3
  Prompt: Why is the Circle of Willis clinically important?
  TargetStructureId: 
  LabelText: 
  Options:
  - It can reroute blood if one supplying artery becomes blocked
  - It stores oxygenated blood for emergencies
  - It filters clots out of the blood
  - It generates the heartbeat
  CorrectOptionIndex: 0
  SequenceSteps: []
  Explanation: Because it is a ring rather than a dead end, flow can arrive at a
    region from more than one direction. This collateral circulation can limit the
    damage from a single blocked vessel.
  Hint: Consider the advantage of a loop over a one-way pipe.
